        "ru-extract.jsonl": [],
        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "77230f8e-08c3-3a1e-9973-5ffba50d3e9a",
                "word": "alweer",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6fa3534b-4da8-32dc-8516-71081eee8020",
                        "entry_id": "77230f8e-08c3-3a1e-9973-5ffba50d3e9a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "opnieuw, nogmaals, wederom, weer"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "919ba56b-3659-488b-be73-d09d74e871d2",
                                "sense_id": "6fa3534b-4da8-32dc-8516-71081eee8020",
                                "text": "'Het geeft niets dat je de som alweer fout hebt gemaakt, we gaan het gewoon nog een keer proberen' zei de geduldige juffrouw tegen het teleurgestelde kind."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9116a5e-71bb-4545-9049-5b2808482501",
                                "sense_id": "6fa3534b-4da8-32dc-8516-71081eee8020",
                                "text": "Natuurlijk, natúúrlijk, werd hij verliefd op een Duitse hippie die op blote voeten op rondreis was door Latijns-Amerika, maar dat was voordat hij zich realiseerde in welk schril contrast zij stond met de plek waar ze vandaan kwam: Frankfurt am Main. Hij had het daar nog geen twee maanden volgehouden of hij vertrok alweer, afgeschrikt door het decor waarin zijn liefdesleven zich moest afspelen - zonder haar, want zij wilde haar leven een wat stabielere wending geven."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88c79dab-5ae6-4306-9c7a-cced28703e02",
                                "sense_id": "6fa3534b-4da8-32dc-8516-71081eee8020",
                                "text": "Twee dagen later bood de volgende verleiding zich alweer aan: Casa de Luna. Het op een bord langs de weg geschreven zinnetje ’Er zijn twee soorten hikers: zij die naar Casa de Luna zijn geweest en zij die ervan balen dat ze niet zijn gegaan’, sprak boekdelen."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1c6af7d2-e2ba-4fda-bb27-5befddc72442",
                        "source_entry_id": "77230f8e-08c3-3a1e-9973-5ffba50d3e9a",
                        "source_sense_id": "6fa3534b-4da8-32dc-8516-71081eee8020",
                        "target_lang_word": "schon wieder",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dfb891ef-b4a7-4b6e-a1bc-d42cfa1358d9",
                        "source_entry_id": "77230f8e-08c3-3a1e-9973-5ffba50d3e9a",
                        "source_sense_id": "6fa3534b-4da8-32dc-8516-71081eee8020",
                        "target_lang_word": "again",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "again",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fabb4b91-a516-3324-9880-444a7c2951e8",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Another time: indicating a repeat of an action."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4cc4570-c7ed-49c3-a1ee-0b763bcf5a85",
                                                "sense_id": "fabb4b91-a516-3324-9880-444a7c2951e8",
                                                "text": "I enjoyed it so much I went again the next day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a9a7d37-55fa-4f00-8cd3-00380bdbb3c6",
                                                "sense_id": "fabb4b91-a516-3324-9880-444a7c2951e8",
                                                "text": "He tangled in tree-tops again and again / And barely missed hitting a tri-motored plane."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04ea94a7-965d-4bff-a5da-f117da7d4b7d",
                                                "sense_id": "fabb4b91-a516-3324-9880-444a7c2951e8",
                                                "text": "Johnny said, “Devil, just come on back if you ever want to try again / I done told you once, you son of a bitch, I’m the best that’s ever been.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3910f14c-c6f5-4ea7-a807-2e748e9fd0b2",
                                                "sense_id": "fabb4b91-a516-3324-9880-444a7c2951e8",
                                                "text": "The last sentence is so shocking, I have to read it again."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9bd39354-3a2d-3424-876b-e75eb622f1a2",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Back (to a former place or state)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30992e29-9f33-485e-beb9-d575955b3883",
                                                "sense_id": "9bd39354-3a2d-3424-876b-e75eb622f1a2",
                                                "text": "We need to bring the old customs to life again."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c96346f4-cb42-4a0c-a02a-9ee82ef2c950",
                                                "sense_id": "9bd39354-3a2d-3424-876b-e75eb622f1a2",
                                                "text": "The South will rise again."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fbcc875-269a-48bf-97d6-3ca6cb5f892b",
                                                "sense_id": "9bd39354-3a2d-3424-876b-e75eb622f1a2",
                                                "text": "The humor of my proposition appealed more strongly to Miss Trevor than I had looked for, and from that time forward she became her old self again;[…]. Our table in the dining-room became again the abode of scintillating wit and caustic repartee, Farrar bracing up to his old standard, and the demand for seats in the vicinity rose to an animated competition."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6ee445a-6054-4084-91d5-7e54597cce7d",
                                                "sense_id": "9bd39354-3a2d-3424-876b-e75eb622f1a2",
                                                "text": "Thinks I to myself, “Sol, you're run off your course again. This is a rich man's summer ‘cottage’[…].[…].” So I started to back away again into the bushes. But I hadn't backed more'n a couple of yards when I see something so amazing that I couldn't help scooching down behind the bayberries and looking at it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6cb36d3d-8e85-485b-b0ff-3ffeff2c4a73",
                                                "sense_id": "9bd39354-3a2d-3424-876b-e75eb622f1a2",
                                                "text": "Meanwhile Nanny Broome was recovering from her initial panic and seemed anxious to make up for any kudos she might have lost, by exerting her personality to the utmost. She took the policeman's helmet and placed it on a chair, and unfolded his tunic to shake it and fold it up again for him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "abb1008c-5137-34f3-b5e8-be42e6a4b9ab",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Over and above a factor of one."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "404450c2-241c-4049-a8ee-0116bf900d69",
                                                "sense_id": "abb1008c-5137-34f3-b5e8-be42e6a4b9ab",
                                                "text": "This stick is quite long, but that other one is half as long again."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e317640d-1229-4d5d-a101-3932ba3211ef",
                                                "sense_id": "abb1008c-5137-34f3-b5e8-be42e6a4b9ab",
                                                "text": "Cirri l-lxxx, 15, about 12mm. long; first two joints short, about twice as broad as long; third about one-third again [=one and one-third times] as long as broad; fourth and fifth the longest, about half again [=one and a half times] as long as broad;[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2bce1eb-54ec-3d1b-824e-5f858438f539",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used metalinguistically, with the repetition being in the discussion, or in the linguistic or pragmatic context of the discussion, rather than in the subject of discussion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab180a69-a0ca-45c0-aefe-d058eb334cd3",
                                                "sense_id": "a2bce1eb-54ec-3d1b-824e-5f858438f539",
                                                "text": "Great, thanks again!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b86c1ae-4e61-3896-b3dc-39738d0da043",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used metalinguistically, with the repetition being in the discussion, or in the linguistic or pragmatic context of the discussion, rather than in the subject of discussion.",
                                            "Tell me again, say again; used in asking a question to which one may have already received an answer that one cannot remember."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a69ba5a7-8466-44ba-b67d-6e8e19065983",
                                                "sense_id": "4b86c1ae-4e61-3896-b3dc-39738d0da043",
                                                "text": "What's that called again?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f161c97e-670a-3505-8c6b-610ccc18b487",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used metalinguistically, with the repetition being in the discussion, or in the linguistic or pragmatic context of the discussion, rather than in the subject of discussion.",
                                            "I ask again, I say again; used in repeating a question or statement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15691318-35a9-4220-ad8a-332a01f2c2c4",
                                                "sense_id": "f161c97e-670a-3505-8c6b-610ccc18b487",
                                                "text": "Again, I'm not criticizing, I just want to understand."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cabea69-b8f5-3dbb-b7eb-dcd5bb3f8c6d",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used metalinguistically, with the repetition being in the discussion, or in the linguistic or pragmatic context of the discussion, rather than in the subject of discussion.",
                                            "Here too, here also, in this case as well; used in applying a previously made point to a new instance; sometimes preceded by \\\"here\\\"."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "900732cd-3ac1-48f2-9431-8372c07d60ac",
                                                "sense_id": "0cabea69-b8f5-3dbb-b7eb-dcd5bb3f8c6d",
                                                "text": "Approach B is better than approach A in many respects, but again, there are difficulties in implementing it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2c72264-e531-44ac-a6d9-5edbec3f7ba8",
                                                "sense_id": "0cabea69-b8f5-3dbb-b7eb-dcd5bb3f8c6d",
                                                "text": "A great bargain also had been the excellent Axminster carpet which covered the floor; as, again, the arm-chair in which Bunting now sat forward, staring into the dull, small fire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f824f2ec-6382-388a-b7a1-0e45ed28609d",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Back in the reverse direction, or to an original starting point."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3985dbc-c234-4f10-8af7-339c3cf881d1",
                                                "sense_id": "f824f2ec-6382-388a-b7a1-0e45ed28609d",
                                                "text": "Bring us word again."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52737c11-c6d2-41a3-bc72-a3d43fdcddcc",
                                                "sense_id": "f824f2ec-6382-388a-b7a1-0e45ed28609d",
                                                "text": "And after they were warned in ther slepe, that they shulde not go ageyne to Herod, they retourned into ther awne countre another way."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e53e530f-9c54-3e5c-8335-5d59365a64f9",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In return, as a reciprocal action; back."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a8d7876-a6de-4fc2-ae6a-04830912bcb4",
                                                "sense_id": "e53e530f-9c54-3e5c-8335-5d59365a64f9",
                                                "text": "So women are never angrie, but to the end a man should againe be angrie with them, therein imitating the lawes of Love."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe3a3b2c-f414-4516-8b71-b4af7c092093",
                                                "sense_id": "e53e530f-9c54-3e5c-8335-5d59365a64f9",
                                                "text": "Thus men are plagued with women, they again with men, when they are of diverse humours and conditions[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10545c5f-6473-45cd-976f-20fc46dca937",
                                                "sense_id": "e53e530f-9c54-3e5c-8335-5d59365a64f9",
                                                "text": "As he lies in the light before a glaring white target, the black upon him shines again[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a9056d8f-f33d-32ae-9ee9-d2bd799de5a9",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In any other place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60842973-7e43-499c-9911-0683f7addc79",
                                                "sense_id": "a9056d8f-f33d-32ae-9ee9-d2bd799de5a9",
                                                "text": "There is not, in the world again, such a spring and seminary of brave military people as in England, Scotland, and Ireland."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c3319fd-2d60-39b8-9bdc-22630c4d051a",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "On the other hand."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcdbe21f-6715-4003-99c6-9d9d6a98111a",
                                                "sense_id": "0c3319fd-2d60-39b8-9bdc-22630c4d051a",
                                                "text": "The one is my sovereign[…]the other again is my kinsman."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8165f695-8a3d-3481-a352-24d30f8c0d87",
                                        "entry_id": "ada406d8-b978-3e1b-b973-ada4b75057a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Moreover; besides; further."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55dfabc9-4838-45eb-9caa-b60962a56166",
                                                "sense_id": "8165f695-8a3d-3481-a352-24d30f8c0d87",
                                                "text": "Again, it is of great consequence to avoid, etc."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "again",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43b1937b-ac97-3a18-a814-ddb8287e0a22",
                                        "entry_id": "18dd4a86-06de-3586-88f8-01ac2703b0a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Against."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f17b9c4-0859-4935-9b0a-045d786d09fc",
                                                "sense_id": "43b1937b-ac97-3a18-a814-ddb8287e0a22",
                                                "text": "And here begynneth the treson of Kynge Marke that he ordayned agayne Sir Trystram."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fc2214b-51a9-4377-b7f6-ad543970023c",
                                                "sense_id": "43b1937b-ac97-3a18-a814-ddb8287e0a22",
                                                "text": "Ah'd like to wahrn (warn) thi agaan 'evvin owt to dew wi' that chap."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b66b91f4-fd15-4e51-a9aa-c79d948abe76",
                                                "sense_id": "43b1937b-ac97-3a18-a814-ddb8287e0a22",
                                                "text": "You may think you are all on the same side, agin the government."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "10f871a7-1f55-4593-8ee8-354c75466a63",
                        "source_entry_id": "77230f8e-08c3-3a1e-9973-5ffba50d3e9a",
                        "source_sense_id": "6fa3534b-4da8-32dc-8516-71081eee8020",
                        "target_lang_word": "de nouveau",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "de nouveau",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f953c474-c219-3919-8b5e-b0a8c01e8f35",
                                        "entry_id": "197e4a05-2a2c-3ef1-a007-742ac4c67b49",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Une fois de plus, encore une fois."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51eadf56-fd0b-464b-a0ac-91ea46b7bb21",
                                                "sense_id": "f953c474-c219-3919-8b5e-b0a8c01e8f35",
                                                "text": "[…]; il ôtait son grand habit noisette, remettait sa perruque dans la boîte et tirait de nouveau son bonnet de soie sur ses oreilles, en disant : […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fc6fbb4-9744-42a9-883e-ce6443bc5156",
                                                "sense_id": "f953c474-c219-3919-8b5e-b0a8c01e8f35",
                                                "text": "Cette parole, dite spontanément et avec candeur, me fit comprendre que tout était vrai dans le récit de Mongenod ; je lui tendis alors la main, et nous nous embrassâmes de nouveau."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93eb3876-5ee5-4760-9734-707fbb5b847d",
                                                "sense_id": "f953c474-c219-3919-8b5e-b0a8c01e8f35",
                                                "text": "Supprimé en 1870, rétabli par l'Assemblée nationale, le cautionnement est de nouveau supprimé pour tous les journaux sans distinction, par la loi de 1881."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ca2a647-2915-4ee2-a09f-1c0bf52c84f6",
                                                "sense_id": "f953c474-c219-3919-8b5e-b0a8c01e8f35",
                                                "text": "La brume nous enveloppa de nouveau, bien que le soleil brillât dans une échappée de ciel au dessus de nos têtes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4283f06a-72d9-42f0-afd6-7599e5eaaea9",
                                                "sense_id": "f953c474-c219-3919-8b5e-b0a8c01e8f35",
                                                "text": "Le ciel s’est nettoyé de tous nuages. Le bleu de la nuit glacée pèse sur les vitres, gicle dans la voiture, ternit le pare-brise, fleurit de diamants les glaces arrière. Bazalo se penche sur le volant pour déchiffrer la route. Le point rouge de sa cigarette danse au dehors, devant lui, au milieu d’une ronde d’étoiles. Les phares promènent une étroite lumière sur la neige éblouie qui s’ensevelit de nouveau sous la nuit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1f971a5-33b4-446b-8129-ff81db38cc6b",
                                                "sense_id": "f953c474-c219-3919-8b5e-b0a8c01e8f35",
                                                "text": "En hésitant beaucoup, elle finit par expliquer que depuis quelques jours les hommes de l’île les harcelaient de nouveau."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "668bccf4-3c5d-4ed0-8a47-7c1e6fd8678b",
                        "source_entry_id": "77230f8e-08c3-3a1e-9973-5ffba50d3e9a",
                        "source_sense_id": "6fa3534b-4da8-32dc-8516-71081eee8020",
